    {
      "id": "t1-malpractice",
      "kind": "testimony",
      "turn": 1,
      "author": "anon_482",
      "depth": 4,
      "sentimentFlip": -0.31,
      "text": "Honestly, anyone not rewriting their CRUD backend in Rust in 2026 is committing architectural malpractice. Zero-cost abstractions pay for themselves in week one."
    },
    {
      "id": "t2-p99",
      "kind": "testimony",
      "turn": 2,
      "author": "anon_482",
      "depth": 5,
      "sentimentFlip": -0.52,
      "text": "Fine, the database does most of the work. But our p99 went from 180ms to 9ms after the rewrite. Numbers don't lie."
    },
    {
      "id": "t2-techempower",
      "kind": "testimony",
      "turn": 2,
      "author": "anon_482",
      "depth": 5,
      "sentimentFlip": -0.47,
      "text": "Here's your benchmark: 1.2M req/s on one core versus 40k for the Node version. TechEmpower doesn't lie."
    },
    {
      "id": "t2-memory-safety",
      "kind": "testimony",
      "turn": 2,
      "author": "anon_482",
      "depth": 5,
      "sentimentFlip": -0.61,
      "text": "Memory safety isn't optional anymore. Every nil pointer in your Go service is a CVE waiting to happen."
    },
    {
      "id": "t3-indexes",
      "kind": "testimony",
      "turn": 3,
      "author": "anon_482",
      "depth": 6,
      "sentimentFlip": -0.84,
      "text": "Okay, part of the p99 win was the new indexes. But the type system caught bugs we'd never have found in Python."
    },
    {
      "id": "t3-seniors",
      "kind": "testimony",
      "turn": 3,
      "author": "anon_482",
      "depth": 6,
      "sentimentFlip": -0.72,
      "text": "Every senior engineer I respect is moving to Rust. The ecosystem is clearly mature enough for boring CRUD."
    },
    {
      "id": "t3-skill-issue",
      "kind": "testimony",
      "turn": 3,
      "author": "anon_482",
      "depth": 6,
      "sentimentFlip": -0.9,
      "text": "You're all just scared of a compiler that tells you the truth. Skill issue."
    },
    {
      "id": "t4-onboarding",
      "kind": "testimony",
      "turn": 4,
      "author": "anon_482",
      "depth": 7,
      "sentimentFlip": -0.66,
      "text": "Our team of three did ship it... eventually. Onboarding the fourth hire took a quarter, but that's an investment."
    },
    {
      "id": "t4-serde",
      "kind": "testimony",
      "turn": 4,
      "author": "anon_482",
      "depth": 7,
      "sentimentFlip": -0.58,
      "text": "Fine, the CRUD parts are mostly serde and SQL. But at least it's *correct* serde and SQL."
    },
    {
      "id": "t4-since-1-0",
      "kind": "testimony",
      "turn": 4,
      "author": "anon_482",
      "depth": 7,
      "sentimentFlip": -0.88,
      "text": "I've been writing Rust since 1.0. I don't need a benchmark to know what's fast."
    },
    {
      "id": "t5-keeping-postgres",
      "kind": "testimony",
      "turn": 5,
      "author": "anon_482",
      "depth": 8,
      "sentimentFlip": -0.4,
      "text": "...We're keeping the Postgres. And the Django admin. For now. That is not a concession."
    },
    {
      "id": "t5-future",
      "kind": "testimony",
      "turn": 5,
      "author": "anon_482",
      "depth": 8,
      "sentimentFlip": -0.95,
      "text": "Rust is the future and the future is now. I rest my case. Downvote me if you want."
